<TUV xml:lang='en-US' struct='1'><PARA><FC tcol='0'>For more details</FC>
<FC tcol='0'> refer to SD.00015/02, /02 and /03.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0' b='1'>Header Size: </FC>
<FC tcol='0'>The fileHeader contains information about the contents of the block as well as all cryptographic hashes and signatures in which to be validated against during block verification.	</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0' b='1'>File Size:</FC>
<FC tcol='0'> The fileSize field defines the length in bytes of the fileData block.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0' b='1'>File Digest:</FC>
<FC tcol='0'> The fileDigest field defines the SHA-256 [FIPS 180-4] calculated over the fileData block.	</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0' b='1'>Subject Name: </FC>
<FC tcol='0'>The targetName field is an identifier for the intended ECU or ECU sub-component for which the signed block is intended.	</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0' b='1'>Subject Key Identifier:</FC>
<FC tcol='0'> The signingKeyIdentifier field contains the subjectKeyIdentifier of the signing certificate.	</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0' b='1'>ECU Type:</FC>
<FC tcol='0'> Type of ECU	</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0' b='1'>RollBack ID:</FC>
<FC tcol='0'> The rollbackId field represents an incremental identifier to prevent known venerable blocks to be used by an ECU.	</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0' b='1'>Compatibility ID:</FC>
<FC tcol='0'> The compatibilityId is a mechanism to ensure that only supported software is run within the ECU.	</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0' b='1'>UUID:</FC>
<FC tcol='0'> The uuid field represents a unique identifier of the signed block.	</FC>
</PARA>
</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' struct='1'><PARA><FC tcol='0'>For more details</FC>
