<DIAGINST id='_00000251D48A2890' oid='67E04401A7B741c8AF7C45CCC7682BF1' tmplref='_00000251D421BFF0' req='notReq'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Plant Mode status</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Plant Mode status</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US' struct='1'><PARA><ATTACHPROXY idref='_00000251CE7B61F0'/>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>This parameter is used to Activate/Deactivate some functions of the Vehicle as requested by Plant, for more details see VF230.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>Is possible manage the Plant Mode Status in order to Activate/Deactivate some funcions (</FC>
<FC b='1' fs='200'>zz</FC>
<FC fs='200'>) under described.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>i.e.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>The data provided by the diagnostic request $3F FF shall be stored in the non-volatile memory each time the valid request arrives.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>The procedure writes data to NVM. This cannot be performed when battery voltage drops below 8,5 V. If this case happen the expected behavior is NRC $93 (Voltage Too Low).</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>This procedure cannot be performed during Cranking and if the vehicle conditions are other than those mentioned in VF616 (1.11.1.1 ECU Algorithm Requirements). If this case happen the expected behavior is NRC $22 (Conditions Not Correct).</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC b='1' u='1' fs='200'>NOTE</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>1.	Default value of RDI $3FFF is $00 00 (Plant Mode disabled and unlocked).</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>2.	Plant Mode can be DISABLED :</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>·	if command $2E 3F FF 00 00 is sent.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>3.	Plant Mode can be LOCKED in following cases:</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>·	if $2E 3F FF 00 80 command is sent (Byte1 bit7 = 1), independently of Plant Mode status, the Plant Mode will be LOCKED and it will be not possible to enable again writing Byte1 bit7 = 0 (in this case, if “Plant Mode odometer locking value” does not exceed the limit, it shall be possible to unlock the Plant Mode using the security access levels $41 and $42 - see point #5 below for more details)  </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>·	If some functions have been enabled and it is needed to lock the Plant Mode, the tool must sent the command $2E 3F FF 00 80 putting to zero all bits from Byte0 bit0 to Byte1 bit6. The ECU shall accept the Plant Mode locking command (Byte1 bit7 = 1) only if writing command contains all other bits (from Byte0 bit0 to Byte1 bit6) set to zero (the previous function enabled will be reset to default). If tool sends for example $2E 3F FF 30 80, the ECU shall answer nack $31 (Request out of range). </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>·	if Total Odometer is equal or higher than the value set in RDI $3FFE “Plant Mode odometer locking value” (in this case RDI $3FFF will assume value $00 80 - Locked and it will be not possible to enable again the Plant Mode, even if using the security access levels $41 and $42).</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>·	The bit set in “Reserved” must be set to 0 value as default. If some funcion will be enabled, putting the “Reserved” bit = 1 (like an error) the ECU shall answer nack $31 (Request out of range).</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>4.	If the vehicle speed exceeds the limit set in RDI $3FFD “Vehicle speed limit for Plant Mode activation”, it shall not be possible to enable the Plant Mode and the ECU shall answer nack $88 (Vehicle Speed Too High) in case of RDI $3FFF writing command (independently from the value). </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>5.	If Plant Mode has been locked by $2E 3F FF 00 80 command (so Byte1 bit7 = 1) and Total Odometer value is lower than the value set in RDI $3FFE “Plant Mode odometer locking value”, it shall be possible to enable again the Plant Mode by following commands:</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>·	perform the security access unlocking in Extended Diagnostic Session:</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>-	$27 41			* security level “41”</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>-	$27 42 + 4 bytes (key)	* security level “42”</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>·	send $2E 3F FF 00 00 command in order to unlock the Plant Mode (Byte1 bit7 = 0, Plant Mode unlocked)</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>·	If Total Odometer value is equal or higher than the value set in RDI $3FFE “Plant Mode odometer locking value” (so Byte1 bit7 = 1) it shall not be possible to enable the Plant Mode again by security access (in this case the ECU shall answer nack $22 - Conditions not correct). </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>6.	If a “Plant Mode” command is done when the Logistic Mode is active [RDI $2949 “State Logistic Mode” = 0x01 - Logistic Mode active] the ECU shall answer with nack $22 - Conditions not correct.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0' fs='200'>7.	If “Plant Mode” is in locked state (62 3F FF 00 80) and a valid command different from the Unlock or </FC>
<FC fs='200'>different from </FC>
<FC tcol='0' fs='200'>another Lock will be request, (IE. 2E 3F FF 01 00) the ECU shall answer nack $24 Request sequence error</FC>
<FC tcol='0' fs='220'>.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>See VF616_V1 (“ECU Algoritm Requiremens” paragraph) for further information</FC>
</PARA>
</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0' struct='1'><PARA><FC fs='200'>This parameter is used to Activate/Deactivate some functions of the Vehicle as requested by Plant. </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>Is possible manage the Plant Mode Status in order to Activate/Deactivate some funcions (</FC>
<FC b='1' fs='200'>zz</FC>
<FC fs='200'>) under described.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>i.e.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>In order to disable the DRL and IAM the command $2E 3FFF 30 00 should be sent (Byte0 bit4 = 1 and Byte0 bit5 = 1).</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>In order to use the Routine 0x0200 “</FC>
<FC tcol='0' fs='200'>Ignition ON by diagnostic tool” </FC>
<FC fs='200'>when the BCM is locked, the command </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>$2E 3FFF 80 00 should be sent. (Byte0 bit7 = 1)</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>The data provided by the diagnostic request $3F FF shall be stored in the non-volatile memory each time the valid request arrives.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>The procedure writes data to NVM. This cannot be performed when battery voltage drops below 8,5 V. If this case happen the expected behavior is NRC $93 (Voltage Too Low).</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>This procedure cannot be performed during Cranking and if the vehicle conditions are other than those mentioned in VF616 (1.11.1.1 ECU Algorithm Requirements). If this case happen the expected behavior is NRC $22 (Conditions Not Correct).</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC b='1' u='1' fs='200'>NOTE</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>1.	Default value of RDI $3FFF is $00 00 (Plant Mode disabled and unlocked).</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>2.	Plant Mode can be DISABLED :</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>·	if command $2E 3F FF 00 00 is sent.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>·	If Logistic Mode is activated [RDI $2949 “State Logistic Mode” = 0x01 - Logistic Mode active], Plant Mode is automatically disabled and RDI $3FFF assumes value $00 00 (Plant Mode disabled and Unlocked - all bit = 0) or $00 80 (Plant Mode disabled and Locked - only Byte1 bit7 = 1),  in this case the Plant Mode was already locked by diagnostic tool or the value set in RDI $3FFE “Plant Mode odometer locking value” exceed the limit set.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>3.	Plant Mode can be LOCKED in following cases:</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>·	if $2E 3F FF 00 80 command is sent (Byte1 bit7 = 1), independently of Plant Mode status, the Plant Mode will be LOCKED and it will be not possible to enable again writing Byte1 bit7 = 0 (in this case, if “Plant Mode odometer locking value” does not exceed the limit, it shall be possible to unlock the Plant Mode using the security access levels $41 and $42 - see point #5 below for more details)  </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>·	If some functions have been enabled and it is needed to lock the Plant Mode, the tool must sent the command $2E 3F FF 00 80 putting to zero all bits from Byte0 bit0 to Byte1 bit6. The ECU shall accept the Plant Mode locking command (Byte1 bit7 = 1) only if writing command contains all other bits (from Byte0 bit0 to Byte1 bit6) set to zero (the previous function enabled will be reset to default). If tool sends for example $2E 3F FF 30 80, the ECU shall answer nack $31 (Request out of range). </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>·	if Total Odometer is equal or higher than the value set in RDI $3FFE “Plant Mode odometer locking value” (in this case RDI $3FFF will assume value $00 80 - Locked and it will be not possible to enable again the Plant Mode, even if using the security access levels $41 and $42).</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>·	The bit set in “Reserved” must be set to 0 value as default. If some funcion will be enabled, putting the “Reserved” bit = 1 (like an error) the ECU shall answer nack $31 (Request out of range).</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>4.	If the vehicle speed exceeds the limit set in RDI $3FFD “Vehicle speed limit for Plant Mode activation”, it shall not be possible to enable the Plant Mode and the ECU shall answer nack $88 (Vehicle Speed Too High) in case of RDI $3FFF writing command (independently from the value). </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>5.	If Plant Mode has been locked by $2E 3F FF 00 80 command (so Byte1 bit7 = 1) and Total Odometer value is lower than the value set in RDI $3FFE “Plant Mode odometer locking value”, it shall be possible to enable again the Plant Mode by following commands:</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>·	perform the security access unlocking in Extended Diagnostic Session:</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>-	$27 41			* security level “41”</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>-	$27 42 + 4 bytes (key)	* security level “42”</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>·	send $2E 3F FF 00 00 command in order to unlock the Plant Mode (Byte1 bit7 = 0, Plant Mode unlocked)</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>·	If Total Odometer value is equal or higher than the value set in RDI $3FFE “Plant Mode odometer locking value” (so Byte1 bit7 = 1) it shall not be possible to enable the Plant Mode again by security access (in this case the ECU shall answer nack $22 - Conditions not correct). </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>6.	If a “Plant Mode” command is done when the Logistic Mode is active [RDI $2949 “State Logistic Mode” = 0x01 - Logistic Mode active] the ECU shall answer with nack $22 - Conditions not correct.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='200'>See VF616_V1 (“ECU Algoritm Requiremens” paragraph) for further information</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><ATTACHPROXY idref='_00000251CE7B7110'/>
</PARA>
</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Plant_Mode_status</QUAL>
