<DIAGINST id='_00000251D48A2E90' oid='D82F2D802F534e8bBBE1EE2B59F55703' tmplref='_00000251D421C900' req='notReq'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Vehicle Manufacturer ECU Hardware Number</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Vehicle Manufacturer ECU Hardware Number</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US' struct='1'><PARA><FC>This data identifier contains information which is used by the diagnostic tool to determine the Vehicle Manufacturer ECUHardware Number. The ECU hardware number represents the ECU hardware configuration and shall only change if an ECU’s hardware changes. The contents is assigned by vehicle manufacturer and must be left aligned with unused byte filled with 0x20 (ASCII code Blanks).</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>This data identifier shall be programmed at supplier end of line and shall not be updated via flash programming, the off board tool shall not be able to update this parameter directly.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>An ECU shall report the identical information regardless of the current mode of the ECU (application software or bootloader) in all available sessions.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC u='1'>NOTE</FC>
<FC>: The Vehicle Manufacturer ECU Hardware Number describes the ECU hardware regardless of the programmed application software.</FC>
</PARA>
</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' struct='1'><PARA><FC>This data identifier contains information which is used by the diagnostic tool to determine the Vehicle Manufacturer ECUHardware Number. The ECU hardware number represents the ECU hardware configuration and shall only change if an ECU’s hardware changes. The contents is assigned by vehicle manufacturer and must be left aligned with unused byte filled with 0x20 (ASCII code Blanks).</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>This data identifier shall be programmed at supplier end of line and shall not be updated via flash programming, the off board tool shall not be able to update this parameter directly.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>An ECU shall report the identical information regardless of the current mode of the ECU (application software or bootloader) in all available sessions.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC u='1'>NOTE</FC>
<FC>: The Vehicle Manufacturer ECU Hardware Number describes the ECU hardware regardless of the programmed application software.</FC>
</PARA>
</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Vehicle_Manufacturer_ECU_Hardware_Number</QUAL>
<SERVICE id='_00000251D48A1200' oid='8AA15152B81248128AA77A86C1CAFBAD' tmplref='_00000251D4598010' func='1' phys='1' respOnPhys='1' respOnFunc='1' req='0'>
