<DIAGINST id='_00000251D48A5A90' oid='D32E4BBFDE4C44a48E2420CBD0E02305' tmplref='_00000251D421C900' req='notReq'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Vehicle Manufacturer ECU Software Number</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Vehicle Manufacturer ECU Software Number</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US' struct='1'><PARA><FC>This data identifier contains information which is used by the diagnostic tool to determine the Vehicle Manufacturer ECU Software Number assigned by FGA/CG. It represents the version of the complete software configuration (all logical blocks) of an ECU. If not assigned by FGA/CG this will be equal to Supplier ECU Software Number. The contents must be left aligned and unused byte shall be filled with 0x20 (ASCII code Blanks).</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>If a replacement ECU is delivered in an un-programmed state (no valid software) the ECU shall return the Vehicle Manufacturer ECU Hardware Number (0xF191) for this DID, different contents should be requested by OEM.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>This data identifier shall be programmed at supplier end of line and shall be updated during flash programming as part of flash file to reflect the new Vehicle Manufacturer ECUSoftware Number. The off board tool shall not be able to update this parameter directly.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>The ECU shall report the identical information regardless of the current mode (application software or bootloader) in all available sessions.</FC>
</PARA>
</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' struct='1'><PARA><FC>This data identifier contains information which is used by the diagnostic tool to determine the Vehicle Manufacturer ECU Software Number assigned by FGA/CG. It represents the version of the complete software configuration (all logical blocks) of an ECU. If not assigned by FGA/CG this will be equal to Supplier ECU Software Number. The contents must be left aligned and unused byte shall be filled with 0x20 (ASCII code Blanks).
If a replacement ECU is delivered in an un-programmed state (no valid software) the ECU shall return the Vehicle Manufacturer ECU Hardware Number (0xF191) for this DID, different contents should be requested by OEM.
This data identifier shall be programmed at supplier end of line and shall be updated during flash programming as part of flash file to reflect the new Vehicle Manufacturer ECUSoftware Number. The off board tool shall not be able to update this parameter directly.
The ECU shall report the identical information regardless of the current mode (application software or bootloader) in all available sessions.</FC>
</PARA>
</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Vehicle_Manufacturer_ECU_Software_Number</QUAL>
<SERVICE id='_00000251D489F280' oid='D728B2943DD743f39D0D88B1EB5AFB61' tmplref='_00000251D4598010' func='1' phys='1' respOnPhys='1' respOnFunc='1' req='0'>
