<DIAGINST id='_00000251D48A5490' oid='413793AA134E4436A092A99F3D165EBE' tmplref='_00000251D421C900' req='req'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>VIN</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>VIN</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US' struct='1'><PARA><ATTACHPROXY idref='_00000251CE7B6610'/>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC b='1'>VIN ORIGINAL</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0'>The BCM distributes the VIN on the vehicle network. The VIN is used to synchronize the configuration data in the vehicle.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>This data record reflects the Vehicle Identification Number (VIN) of the vehicle an ECU was originally installed.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>The system supplier shall delivery the ECU with F190 hex padded with 0xFF. The management of the DID 0xF190 and 0xF1B0 are defined into VF_607.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>An ECU shall report the identical information regardless of the current mode of the ECU (application software or bootloader) in all available sessions.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>Upon requesting data identifier [F1 90 Hex] with the diagnostic service Read Data By Identifier [22 Hex], the ECU shall return the VIN Original.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>Original VIN (0xF190) can be locked by diagnostic command (routine $200) or in automatic way after 5 km or alternately after 10 key off / key on if CLUSTER1.TotalOdometer is not available</FC>
<FC tcol='255' fs='220'> </FC>
<FC>- see VF_607 for more details.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC b='1' u='1'>Note</FC>
<FC b='1'>:</FC>
<FC> unlocking of original VIN is possible only for Plant by routine $2001 (see this routine for more information).</FC>
</PARA>
</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' struct='1'><PARA><ATTACHPROXY idref='_00000251CE7B6610'/>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC b='1'>VIN ORIGINAL</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0'>The BCM distributes the VIN on the vehicle network. The VIN is used to synchronize the configuration data in the vehicle.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>This data record reflects the Vehicle Identification Number (VIN) of the vehicle an ECU was originally installed.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>The system supplier shall delivery the ECU with F190 hex padded with 0xFF. The management of the DID 0xF190 and 0xF1B0 are defined into VF_607.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>An ECU shall report the identical information regardless of the current mode of the ECU (application software or bootloader) in all available sessions.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>Upon requesting data identifier [F1 90 Hex] with the diagnostic service Read Data By Identifier [22 Hex], the ECU shall return the VIN Original.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>Original VIN (0xF190) can be locked by diagnostic command (routine $200) or in automatic way after 5 km or alternately after 10 key off / key on if CLUSTER1.TotalOdometer is not available</FC>
<FC tcol='255' fs='220'> </FC>
<FC>- see VF_607 for more details.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC b='1' u='1'>Note</FC>
<FC b='1'>:</FC>
<FC> unlocking of original VIN is possible only for Plant by routine $2001 (see this routine for more information).</FC>
</PARA>
</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>VIN</QUAL>
