<DIAGINST id='_00000251D49DEA80' oid='30DFD040A9274ccaBDF464FA3B29658D' tmplref='_00000251D421C900' req='notReq'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>VIN Current</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>VIN Current</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US' struct='1'><PARA><FC bcol='65535' b='1'>NOTE: write command is foreseen only for BCM. For other ECUs the write command must be disabled.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC b='1'>VIN CURRENT</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0'>The BCM distributes the VIN on the vehicle network. The VIN is used to synchronize the configuration data in the vehicle.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>This data record reflects the Vehicle Identification Number of the vehicle an ECU is currently installed.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>The system supplier shall deliver the ECU with F1B0 hex padded with 0xFF. The management of the DID 0xF190 and 0xF1B0 are defined into VF_607.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>Upon requesting data identifier [F1 B0 Hex] with the diagnostic service Read Data By Identifier [22 Hex], the ECU shall return the VIN Current. Upon requesting [F1 B0 Hex], with diagnostic service Write Data by Identifier [2E Hex], the VIN master ECU (BCM) shall write the data transferred in the request message to the associated memory block.</FC>
</PARA>
</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' struct='1'><PARA><FC bcol='65535' b='1'>NOTE: write command is foreseen only for BCM. For other ECUs the write command must be disabled.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC b='1'>VIN CURRENT</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0'>The BCM distributes the VIN on the vehicle network. The VIN is used to synchronize the configuration data in the vehicle.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>This data record reflects the Vehicle Identification Number of the vehicle an ECU is currently installed.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>The system supplier shall deliver the ECU with F1B0 hex padded with 0xFF. The management of the DID 0xF190 and 0xF1B0 are defined into VF_607.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>Upon requesting data identifier [F1 B0 Hex] with the diagnostic service Read Data By Identifier [22 Hex], the ECU shall return the VIN Current. Upon requesting [F1 B0 Hex], with diagnostic service Write Data by Identifier [2E Hex], the VIN master ECU (BCM) shall write the data transferred in the request message to the associated memory block.</FC>
</PARA>
</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>VIN_Current</QUAL>
<SERVICE id='_00000251D496F040' oid='FC9DD645207D45e9979391FAE6286F98' tmplref='_00000251D4598010' func='1' phys='1' respOnPhys='1' respOnFunc='1' req='0'>
