<DIAGINST id='_00000251D49E0080' oid='D60F8DBFF0F44b1cADD56276C897D46E' tmplref='_00000251D421C900' req='notReq'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Vehicle Manufacturer ECU Software Calibration Number</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US' struct='1'><PARA><FC tcol='0'>This data identifier contains information which is used by the diagnostic tool to determine the Vehicle Manufacturer ECU Software Calibration Number assigned by FCA. It represents the version of the only calibration software of the ECU. The SW Calibration Number can include a maximum of ten (10) characters. SW Calibration Number shall contain only printable ASCII characters and will be reported as ASCII values. The contents is assigned by vehicle manufacturer and must be left aligned with unused byte filled with $20 (ASCII code Blanks). </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0'>If not assigned (for example during the development phase) this will be filled with $20 (ASCII code Blanks). </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0'>This data identifier shall be programmed at supplier end of line and shall be updated during flash programming as part of flash file to reflect the new Vehicle Manufacturer ECU Software Calibration Number. It shall be updated immediately at the end of the download without necessity to perform an Ignition OFF / Ignition ON. The off board tool shall not be able to update this parameter directly by write service. </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0'>This Identification must be supported in all diagnostic sessions including boot. </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0'>DID $F18A (Vehicle Manufacturer ECU Software Number) must be updated immediately at the end of the download without necessity to perform an Ignition OFF / Ignition ON. </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0'>In case of interrupted download the previous value must be maintaned.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0'>$F18A values are provided by ESLM (by CVVR document, CVVR header sheet in OEM ID Number field).</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC b='1'>NOTE</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>This parameter must be available also in boot, so it must be possible to read this parameter by service $22 also with ECU in boot condition.</FC>
</PARA>
</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' struct='1'></TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Vehicle_Manufacturer_ECU_Hardware_Number_1</QUAL>
