<TRRECORDITEM idref='_00000251D41D2180'>
<TEXT>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>***** Engineering Notes*****

***** Customer Perception Symptom*****

***** Possible Causes*****
a) CAN PINs unstable or loosen
b) CAN bus in short circuit
c) Power supply wrongly
d) Transceiver CAN not work correctly
***** Repair Action*****
a) Restore the correct functionality of the PINs or connectors and their location as well
b) Restore CAN network continuity and correct isolation of the CAN network
c) Restore or, if necessary, replace the power supply harness
d) Perform a second level analysis OR If the fault persists replace the ECU .
</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</TEXT>
</TRRECORDITEM>
