<RECORD id='_00000251D4A7E060' oid='181F1658A42748d680AF05C7BB0BD805' v='14090374'>
<TEXT>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Body Control Module (BCM) - Signal invalid</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</TEXT>
<TRRECORDITEM idref='_00000251D41D2180'>
<TEXT>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>***** Engineering Notes*****

***** Customer Perception Symptom*****

***** Possible Causes*****
a) BCM
b) CAN PINs connected to ECC unstable or loosen
c) CAN PINs connected to BCM unstable or loosen
d) Short circuit in the CAN bus harness between ECC and BCM
***** Repair Action*****
a) Verify if BCM is not receiving or sending a signal
b) c) Restore the correct functionality of the PINs or connectors and their location as well.
d) Restore or, if necessary, replace the harness OR If the fault persists replace the ECU.
</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</TEXT>
</TRRECORDITEM>
<TRRECORDITEM idref='_00000251D41D0D40'>
<TEXT>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>***** Maturation Vehicle Conditions*****
I_ON;I_EO
***** Maturation Fault Detection Conditions*****
ENABLE CONDITIONS:
Test executed if: 
8V &#60; VBatt &#60; 16V 
- BCM TINIT Phase Ended
- NO BCM DTC Node Absent present
***** Maturation Failure Threshold*****
FAULT DETECTION CONDITIONS:
Error detected if: 
At least one of the messages of the node does have a shorter length than specified:
BCM_COMMAND
BODY1
BODY2
BODY3
BODY4
C2_IGW3
RFHUB2
VIN
BCM_VPS2
BODY11
EXTERNAL LIGHT
STATUS_BH_BCM1
STATUS_BH_BCM2
STATUS_BH_BCM3
STATUS_CCAN8
STATUS_LIN
STATUS_PAM
STATUS_UBSS_BH
STATUS_HCP
STATUS_TSR
GE
HAPTIC1
HAPTIC2

***** Maturation Time*****
2500 ms
</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</TEXT>
</TRRECORDITEM>
