<DIAGINST id='_00000251D4B60260' oid='B3982FDF78104793BAF01143CC6C2441' tmplref='_00000251D45A39E0' req='notReq'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Reset Odometer</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Reset Odometer</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US' struct='1'><PARA><FC b='1'>see VF023 for major dettails.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0' i='1' fs='200'>The IPC must be delivered to the assembly plant having </FC>
<FC tcol='0' i='1' u='1' fs='200'>one only</FC>
<FC tcol='0' i='1' fs='200'> total odometer reset possibility, within the first 200 km (or the equivalent in miles) covered. The possibility to execute such reset must be indicated by the presence of the “H“ letter on the first digit on the left.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0' i='1' fs='200'>If total odometer reset operation (pressing the dedicated key or the “Trip” key for a time of t &#62; 5 s)</FC>
<FC tcol='0' b='1' i='1' fs='200'> </FC>
<FC tcol='0' i='1' fs='200'>is executed before covering 200 km (or the equivalent in miles), total odometer is resetted and the “H” letter disappears. If such operation is not executed before covering 200 km instead (or the equivalent in miles), the “H” letter automatically disappears and the km (or miles) covered are maintained and displayed, losing the possibility to reset total odometer.</FC>
</PARA>
</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' struct='1'><PARA><FC b='1'>see VF023 for major dettails.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0' i='1' fs='200'>The IPC must be delivered to the assembly plant having </FC>
<FC tcol='0' i='1' u='1' fs='200'>one only</FC>
<FC tcol='0' i='1' fs='200'> total odometer reset possibility, within the first 200 km (or the equivalent in miles) covered. The possibility to execute such reset must be indicated by the presence of the “H“ letter on the first digit on the left.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='0' i='1' fs='200'>If total odometer reset operation (pressing the dedicated key or the “Trip” key for a time of t &#62; 5 s)</FC>
<FC tcol='0' b='1' i='1' fs='200'> </FC>
<FC tcol='0' i='1' fs='200'>is executed before covering 200 km (or the equivalent in miles), total odometer is resetted and the “H” letter disappears. If such operation is not executed before covering 200 km instead (or the equivalent in miles), the “H” letter automatically disappears and the km (or miles) covered are maintained and displayed, losing the possibility to reset total odometer.</FC>
</PARA>
</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Reset_Odometer</QUAL>
