<DIAGINST id='_00000251D4B61660' oid='A8DD44E3400E44efAF7166B9642D1512' tmplref='_00000251D45A44C0' req='req'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Download</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it'>Download</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US' struct='1'><PARA><FC b='1' u='1' fs='200'>Authenticated Firmware / Secure flashing</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>If Authenticated Firmware / Secure flashing is requested to be implemented for Cyber Security protection (ref. CS.00093) and if flashing flow must be adherent to CS.00053 without additional commands (i.e. signature check routine), signature check result can be included in the checksum routine result (routine $FF 01).</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>All the signature verification (as per CS.00093) shall be performed before checksum calculation. In case of signature verification failure the all new software must be deleted from the flash. The delete operation shall be done before checksum calculation.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>Before start of firmware transmission on ECU the “SW valid bit” bit shall be set to true (refer to DID $2010). The bit may be set to false only after the signature verification and only if the verification is passed.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>In case of CMAC (Cipher Message Authentication Code) protection (ref. CS.00098) is used for secure boot (cs.00093) it shall be calculated only after successful signature verification and anyway before checksum calculation. In case of CMAC calculation error, the checksum shall return wrong.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>If certificates come together with firwmare to be flashed, for the X.509 certificates (ref. SD.00078) download, </FC>
<FC u='1'>possible examples</FC>
<FC> are:</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>1.	The X.509 certificates can be downloaded and validated by the ECU before the actual application / calibration content is erased and reprogrammed (to give a chance to abort without disabling the ECU, if the certificates are not valid). </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>In this case the sequence “Flash erase, transfer data, transfer exit, checksum check” is executed once separately for certificate data, and depending on response from the checksum routine (which also validates the certificates besides doing CRC - check), the tool can then proceed with one more cycle for the firmware content.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>Segment 1 -&#62; Certificate segment: contains the binary and signature</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>Segment 2 -&#62; Real code segment: contains the app/cal binary and signature</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>2.	The X.509 certificates can be downloaded and validated by the ECU together the actual application / calibration content. In this case the sequence “Flash erase, transfer data, transfer exit, checksum check” is executed only one time.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>Segment 1 -&#62; Real code segment: contains the binary of the app/cal, the app/cal’s signature, the certificate and the certificate signature</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC u='1'>Note 1</FC>
<FC>: in both cases the signature is part of the binary that is downloaded.</FC>
<FC tcol='2236962'> </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC u='1'>Note 2</FC>
<FC>: other firmware block formats are possible (to agree with FCA).</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC>According to CS.00053 flash flow, see examples below that summarize which commands the diagnostic tool sends to the ECU in both above cases. </FC>
<FC u='1'>They are only examples, so supplier can implement different solutions.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC bcol='65535' b='1'>CASE 1: flashing example (one segment for the certificate and one segment for the real code)</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends $10 03 in Functional Addressing (so all ECUs enter in Extended Diagnostic Session)</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends ControlDTCOff ($85 02) and CommunicationControlDisabling ($28 01 03) in Functional Addressing (so all ECUs disable the DTC storing and they stop the send Network and Normal Communication messages on CAN)</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends Programming Session command to the ECU</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends Seed&#38;Key commands ($27 01 / 02) to the ECU</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends Fingerprint commands to the ECU according to prm information ($F184 is written if app is going to be flashed; $F185 is written if cal is going to be flashed)     * in this example we consider cal flash only</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962' b='1'>1st cycle / 1st segment</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends flash erase command (routine $FF 00) for the security certificate area</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends download request command ($34) for the security certificate area</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends transfer data command ($36); binary contains certificate and certificate's signature</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends transfer exit command</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends checksum calculation routine ($31 01 FF 01 + start address + stop address + expected checksum) for the security certificate area       * expected checksum value has two bytes length and value is reported in prm file</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends checksum calculation routine result ($31 03 FF 01) for the security certificate area</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- ECU can return these responses:</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>     1.       positive response -&#62; it means that signature and checksum are correct. In this case flashing continues.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>     2.       negative response nack $72 -&#62; it means that signature or checksum are not correct (ECU does not remain in boot and Fingerprint $F185 will return the new value in order to trace the reprogramming attempt). In this case flashing is interrupted. If signature check has failed, bit 1 (Signature failure event in last ECU reprogramming attempt) of DID $E100 shall be set to 1.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962' b='1'>2nd cycle / 2nd segment</FC>
<FC tcol='2236962'>  </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends flash erase command (routine $FF 00) for the cal area</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends download request command ($34) for the cal area</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends transfer data command ($36); binary contains app and app's signature</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends transfer exit command</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends checksum calculation routine ($31 01 FF 01 + start address + stop address + expected checksum) for the cal area       </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>* expected checksum value has two bytes length and value is reported in prm file</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends checksum calculation routine result ($31 03 FF 01) for the cal area</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- ECU can return these responses:</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>     1.       positive response -&#62; it means that signature and checksum are correct</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>     2.       negative response nack $72 -&#62; it means that signature or checksum are not correct (ECU remains in boot and Fingerprint $F185 will return the new value in order to trace the reprogramming attempt). If signature check has failed, bit 1 (Signature failure event in last ECU reprogramming attempt) of DID $E100 shall be set to 1.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends whole checksum calculation routine result ($31 03 FF 01)</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- ECU can return these responses:</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>     1.       positive response -&#62; it means that checksum is correct   * expected checksum value has two bytes length and value is reported in prm file  </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>     2.       negative response nack $72 -&#62; it means that checksum is not correct ECU remains in boot (Fingerprint $F185 will return the new value in order to trace the reprogramming attempt).</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends the ECU reset command ($11 01)</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC bcol='65535' b='1'>CASE 2: flashing example (one segment for both the certificate and for the real code)</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC></FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends $10 03 in Functional Addressing (so all ECUs enter in Extended Diagnostic Session)</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends ControlDTCOff ($85 02) and CommunicationControlDisabling ($28 01 03) in Functional Addressing (so all ECUs disable the DTC storing and they stop the send Network and Normal Communication messages on CAN)</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends Programming Session command to the ECU</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends Seed&#38;Key commands ($27 01 / 02) to the ECU</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends Fingerprint commands to the ECU according to prm information ($F184 is written ifs app is going to be flashed; $F185 is written if cal is going to be flashed)     * in this example we consider app flash only</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends flash erase command (routine $FF 00)</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends download request command ($34)</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends transfer data command ($36); binary contains appl, app's signature, certificate and certificate's signature</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends transfer exit command</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends checksum calculation routine ($31 01 FF 01 + start address + stop address + expected checksum)        * expected chesum value has two bytes length and value is reported in prm file</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends checksum calculation routine result  ($31 03 FF 01)  </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- ECU can return these responses:</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>     1.       positive response -&#62; it means that signature and checksum are correct</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>     2.       negative response nack $72 -&#62; it means that signature or checksum are not correct (ECU remains in boot and Fingerprint $F184 will return the new value in order to trace the reprogramming attempt). If signature check has failed, bit 1 (Signature failure event in last ECU reprogramming attempt) of DID $E100 shall be set to 1.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC tcol='2236962'>- tool sends the ECU reset command ($11 01).</FC>
</PARA>
</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='it' uptodate='0' struct='1'><PARA><FC>

WARNING !!!! The configuration parameters have to be updated according to application.</FC>
</PARA>
</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Download</QUAL>
